r handoff is exempted from that whole block by monitor_handoff_claim_transferred; the gate handoff has no equivalent, and fixing (4) without adding one would turn the harmless hold error into an active release_workspace + clear_occupant_record of the pending gate shell's workspace. Not affected: the SIGTERM path, which already covers every non-monitor handoff marker via run_agent_runner_signals._NON_MONITOR_HANDOFF_MARKERS. A tale plan fixing this is being proposed: share one SHELL_HANDOFF_OUTCOMES constant between the monitor and gate outcomes, use it at all four sites, add a gate analogue of monitor_handoff_claim_transferred keyed on workflow 'ace-gate' (no pid-liveness check, because a pending gate shell has no process and deliberately keeps the dead creator's pid), and add a parity guard test so the next shell kind cannot repeat this."
