"LAND VERIFICATION (sase-p3.land, 2026-08-18, workspace sase_12, master 1ad14c1d1).\n\nVERIFIED COMPLETE. All 14 phases closed resolution=done and their deliverables exist in\nsource, not just in notes: task_type/task_type_fields on the wire + SQLite mirror\n(sase-core 85cc322), spec validation/digest/body rendering (sase-core 82b10b5),\n<plugin>@<id> use: prefix + config.file_hooks doctor check\n(src/sase/doctor/checks_config.py:77 -- it IS registered and runs; the earlier report\nthat `sase doctor -C config.file_hooks` is an unknown check id does NOT reproduce),\nplugins.required + resolver + fail-closed helper, sase_task_types hookspec/discovery/\nregistry + beads.task_types doctor check, five builtin specs + `sase bead task-type\nlist/show`, typed create (`sase bead create -t X -T task` correctly errors \"task beads\nrequire -T 'task(<slug>)'\" and lists the agent-creatable slugs), task_type_presentation\nrouted through 13 surfaces, per-type min_plus_ones, sase/task_types.json +\nsase/memory/task_types.md, the PluginsRequired gate/chop, the github type + mirror\nstamping, and the Task Type / Required Plugin glossary entries (sase/sase.yml, added in\n1ad14c1d1 -- `sase glossary list -p sase` shows only 27 terms because that resolves the\nregistered project's older canonical checkout, not this workspace).\n\nINTEGRATION REVIEWED. 18 non-epic commits landed since 54da09ba5 (glossary panel, sase\npipe, EpicResume gate + epic_resume chop, ACE Ctrl+] repo jump, docs). Nothing in them\nduplicates or conflicts with task types: the only production call site that creates\nIssueType.TASK beads is external_mirror/_issue_apply.py, which already passes\ntask_type=\"github\"; no new `use:` fields were added; the glossary panel does not render\ntask beads; the task-triage gate preview already renders type bodies via\nrender_task_type_display_block.\n\nSTALE FOLLOW-UPS CLEARED (re-verified on this tree, no action needed): the feature-flags\nlint (sase-pa / epic_resume_gate) proposed on .6/.7/.10/.12 now passes\n(tools/check_feature_flags exit 0); the stale --epic-symbol entries proposed on .6\n(sase-p1.7, sase-p3.11, sase-p4.3) are gone and `just _lint-symvision` exits 0 with\n`sase bead epic-symbols sase-p3` reporting no entries; the keymaps help test proposed on\n.6 passes; the home-chezmoi memory drift proposed on .12 does not reproduce\n(`sase memory init --check` flags only sase/task_types.json); and the missing sase-github\nsase_task_types entry point proposed on .13 is fixed upstream -- 0.2.5 is released and\non PyPI. Remaining open follow-ups are flakes not caused by this epic\n(tests/ace/tui/test_logs_pane.py, tests/test_procs_supervisor.py, and the five\nflake-baseline nodes from .14); they stay for the close-out triage pass.\n\nNOT CLOSING. Four epic-caused defects are live on master, all rooted in the\n_setup-required-plugins recipe sase-p3.4 added in 1e59c50e7 (which the plan never asked\nfor -- D7 explicitly routes missing plugins to a doctor ERROR, a fail-closed path, and\nan install gate, not to an unconditional install inside `just install`):\n\n1. EVERY CI JOB ON MASTER FAILS AT \"Install dependencies\". sase-research-artifacts has\n   never been published (its release-please Publish workflow fails every run with\n   \"GitHub Actions is not permitted to create or approve pull requests\"), so the PyPI\n   branch aborts with \"not found in the package registry\". Verified on CI run\n   32115186909 for 1ad14c1d1: lint, test 3.12/3.13/3.14, perf-floors, visual-test,\n   coverage-contexts, and ace-page-group-isolation all die at that one step.\n2. install_one treats \"a dist-info exists\" as \"installed\", so it cannot repair a\n   dangling editable .pth (this workspace's every sase command errored on the\n   research-highlights file hook until I ran `sase repo open`) and cannot move a stale\n   version forward (sase-github stayed at 0.2.4, whose wheel has no sase_task_types\n   entry point, so `github` is absent from the live