tion\n  to name it as owner if the node had to be baselined. The sase-qo entry carries a comment\n  telling whoever commits sase-qd's fix to replace it with a `# fixed-at:` line so the\n  pre-fix evidence retires rather than lingering. These are debt entries, not resolutions."
"LANDED. VERIFIED (step 1): all 8 phases closed done; read every child note and confirmed each was addressed. The epic's own two DISCOVERED ISSUEs are resolved on master — the stale tests/completion/snapshots/cli_spec.json (missing bead epic-symbols) regenerates clean (tools/sync_completion_spec --check exits 0), and live flag bead sase-om now has its registry definition (src/sase/feature_flags/registry.py, key completion_refresh_on_update), so the feature-flags lint gate is green. Read the source behind the phase claims rather than trusting them: entry.py's pre-argparse guard matches the plan's snippet exactly; build/model/shorten/kinds produce the spec all three emitters consume; emit_zsh writes _arguments -C -s -S with exclusion lists, mutex groups, remainders and :kind:{__sase_candidates ...} actions; emit_bash and emit_fish carry the same alias policy and kind markers; install.py resolves a target, writes atomically, zcompiles, probes _comps[sase] and stamps; checks_completion.py registers completion.install and completion.registration; update_handler.py calls maybe_refresh_installed_completions behind the beta flag. Ran the suites: 235 completion/parser/fast-path/contract tests pass (1 skip: fish absent from this host), and a full-suite 'just check' escalation reported 32630 passed with only the two pre-existing tests/test_force_reuse_launch_seam.py failures, reproduced on clean master with my tree stashed and corroborated on task sase-ot (+1). End-to-end on the real host: 'sase completion install zsh' detects, targets, writes, zcompiles, migrates, stamps and verifies _comps[sase]=_sase; a live interactive-zsh pty confirms 'sase bead sh<TAB>' -> 'sase bead show' and 'sase bead show <TAB>' inserting the live candidates' common prefix.\n\nINTEGRATED (step 2): reviewed every non-epic commit since 48856bc89. Three touched CLI surface. f5565edda's root -f/--enable-feature and -F/--disable-feature already resolve to kind flag. f6d757e2c and a383212a2 landed the whole sase glossary group mid-epic with its TERM slots completing as bare files — sase-op.6 recorded exactly that as a PROPOSED FOLLOW-UP ('ValueKind.GLOSSARY was intentionally left unset'). Wired it here: ValueKind.GLOSSARY plus PATH_OVERRIDES for glossary show/read TERM and glossary log -t/--term, and a catalog provider that reads the project's memory.glossary node through yaml_safe_load and offers slug-form references (agent-hood) with each term's shortened definition, plus authored aliases described as 'alias of <Term>'. Slug form is deliberate: sase glossary resolves references case- and separator-insensitively, so a slug is the one shape that never needs shell quoting. The kind holds the fast path's import-set and 150ms budget (added to the contract test's parametrization) and the spec snapshot is regenerated. Recorded the outcome on sase-op so its land agent does not redo it. Also gave 'sase completion candidates KIND' the shipped-kind choices it was missing, so the epic's own command completes its own value kinds.\n\nFIXED (epic-caused): resolve_target picked the first writable scanned directory, which on any oh-my-zsh host is an unrelated enabled plugin's own directory — this epic had installed _sase and _sase.zwc into ~/.oh-my-zsh/plugins/z on athena, where the script would vanish from fpath the day that plugin is disabled. Framework plugin trees and cache roots are now never chosen; a framework's completions drop-in directory is preferred and created when the framework ships the fpath entry without the directory (verified: ~/.oh-my-zsh/custom/completions registers before compinit on this host, while ~/.zfunc is appended after compinit and does not), home directories beat system-wide ones, and a reinstall removes the script a previous install stamped elsewhere so changing targets never leaves a second copy. The stray plugin-directory files are gone. docs/completion.md documents all of it.\n\nFOLLOW-UPS: filed sase-ou (sase/core/__init__.py eager facade imports